1. The OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize checkpoint repository, revision
   10304d926740cf5a5cee05a268086e3265197910:
   https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize

   - runtime/prompt_plan.cpp re-implements the audio chunking, the per-chunk
     audio token count and the time-marker expansion of the audio span
     (_chunk_audio, _compute_audio_token_length, _audio_span_ids in
     processing_moss_transcribe_diarize.py).
   - audio_encoder.py and decoder.py express the network of
     modeling_moss_transcribe_diarize.py (Whisper encoder, frame merge,
     VQAdaptor, Qwen3 decoder with audio placeholder injection) as TensorRT
     graphs; the bundle embeds the repository's weights and tokenizer data.

2. The OpenMOSS MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize package, commit
   79c675f0670cc2f824bcbcdd98263704f40f1f7e:
   https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize

   - runtime/text_output.cpp ports TranscriptStreamParser of
     moss_transcribe_diarize/transcript_parser.py (parse_transcript for the
     "[start][Sxx]text[end]" spans).
   - tokens.py and tests/test_e2e.py carry the default transcription
     instruction (DEFAULT_PROMPT) of moss_transcribe_diarize/inference_utils.py,
     and tests/test_e2e.py follows its prepare_inputs and
     generate_transcription steps for the reference run.

